+/// The `modified` an **overwrite** commits, given the superseded generation's stamp
+/// (`prior`) and the publisher's (`published`): `max(published, prior + 1 ms)`, so a file's
+/// last-modified time never goes backwards across overwrites that each record a time (#768).
+///
+/// Each gateway of an active/active fleet stamps from its own clock, so a prior written by a
+/// gateway whose clock runs fast would otherwise be followed by an earlier stamp on newer
+/// content — and a sync tool comparing size and `Last-Modified` skips a same-size overwrite.
+/// The prior stamp is the one this commit supersedes: both callers CAS on the exact `prior`
+/// bytes, so the ordering is against the generation actually replaced.
+///
+/// - `published == None` → `None`: a generation published with no time records none. The
+///   chain resets there, and the next stamped overwrite starts from its own clock, because
+///   carrying the prior's time forward (or inventing one) would put a time on content its
+///   publisher never stamped. Both gateway PUT paths always stamp one; only core's API can
+///   publish without it.
+/// - `prior == None` (a legacy record, ADR-0047) → the publisher's stamp stands.
+/// - The `+ 1` saturates: a prior of `u64::MAX` (decodable, ADR-0045) stays `u64::MAX`.
+///
+/// Every path that publishes content **over** a prior generation must call this — today
+/// [`commit_chunk_map_superseding`] and [`commit_chunk_map_superseding_leased`]. The multipart
+/// Complete flip (#658) publishes through its own committer (proposal 0016 rules out reusing
+/// the leased one), so it must call this explicitly; it does not inherit it. Repair commits
+/// ([`commit_chunk_map`], reconstruction, backfill, rebalance) re-commit the same content and
+/// keep preserving `modified` unchanged instead.
+pub fn overwrite_modified(prior: Option<u64>, published: Option<u64>) -> Option<u64> {
+    let published = published?;
+    Some(match prior {
+        Some(prior) => published.max(prior.saturating_add(1)),
+        None => published,
+    })
+}
+
